# collisional_starburst_recipe with BulgeSizeOn 3, an instability burst (mode 1) of a real R1
# central into its instability channel, followed by the radius update
# (R/src/model_mergers.c:779-784) with the central's own DiskScaleRadius as old_disk_radius.
# Source: R1 reference /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R1/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256 870acea288250919624ae8a4b984a4dde7106e6355cdb972cf4880ff04635ca0), Snap_32 row 66 (GalaxyIndex 172, Type 0).
# End-of-snapshot output values used as plausible call inputs, not reconstructed call-time
# state. The trigger (an unstable gas fraction of 0.1) is constructed; call.time, call.dt
# and call.step are the R0 template's plausible values.
# SnapNum: the rows store the output snapshot; the galaxies' SnapNum (one less) is a
# constructed call-time value. Constructed: deltaMvir (central +2% of Mvir, satellite -5%),
# the clocks (999.9 for the central, SAGE26's central clock B:288; 0.0 for a satellite, unread),
# OutflowRate 0 (its value after the first-occupied reset, R/src/core_build_model.c:276),
# TimeOfLast*Merger -1 (SAGE26's creation sentinel, R/src/model_misc.c:179-180; unread here)
# and zero histories. Every other galaxy field is the row's output value, which the writer
# stores verbatim.
# Reachability: R1-reachable.
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
routine collisional_starburst_recipe

